<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galway</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galway is a city on the west coast of Ireland, at the mouth of the River Corrib on Galway Bay, and gives its name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>. Founded as an Anglo-Norman town by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-burgh">de Burgh family</a> in the 13th century, it was governed by merchant families known as the Tribes of Galway and traded widely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The surrounding county takes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connemara">Connemara</a> and the old lordships of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oflaherty">O'Flahertys</a> and the Clanricarde Burkes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galway.jpg" alt="Galway" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galway_cathedral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
